            <ArticleTitle>Patients' perception of day case surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>27-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A postal questionnaire was used to assess patient compliance with instructions, post-operative sequelae and general practitioner workload resulting from the day case unit of Daisy Hill Hospital, Newry. Compliance with instructions was good. There was little post-operative pain but there was a high incidence of other side effects. Few patients needed to see their general practitioner in the week following surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
